The file is a frozen snapshot of 1707 events (generated 2018-02-07). It is
small, so sample.jsonl.zst holds all of them, not a subset. Each GeoJSON
feature becomes one record: the constant feature "type" is dropped, time and
updated are read as UTC timestamp-millis, magType is renamed mag_type, and the
comma-delimited ids, sources and types strings (",ci,us,") become string
arrays. Regenerate it with:

    go run ./cmd/fetch -dataset earthquakes
    go test ./datasets/earthquakes -update "$PWD/data/earthquakes/earthquakes.json"
